    descriptionEn: "Paid per hectare for specific crops to maintain processing chains' capacity and the feed supply: oilseeds (rapeseed, sunflower, etc.), seed potatoes, forage-grass, forage-legume and maize seed, soya, grain legumes and sugar beet. Sugar beet grown organically or without plant-protection products gets a supplement. Cereals (wheat, spelt, rye, barley, oats, triticale, rice, millet, sorghum, etc.) also receive a cereal supplement, calculated by dividing the available budget by the eligible cereal area (Single-Crop Contributions Ordinance, EKBV). Source: FOAG, Direct Payments Overview 2026.",
